  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is config_048 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) at 0.6287 accuracy, a large jump over the best singleprofile result (0.5353). This shows multiprofile aggregation is the most impactful design axis. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the simple avgpool aggregation is near-optimal or whether a learned aggregation (transformer) can better capture interactions across profiles. config_039 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding the best RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion constant, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_048. If transformer aggregation yields a meaningful gain, it reveals that cross-profile interactions are exploitable and justifies further investment in richer aggregation; if it does not, avgpool is confirmed as sufficient and the budget is better spent on other axes (e.g., image encoder or fusion). This is the highest-information next step because it directly extends the strongest configuration along the most fundamental untested dimension."
}

